// PARAM: --analysis int --solver join
// Exercises --solver join against the composite integer domain. Int's
// production default is Solver_Warrow at Refine_Fixpoint; join is the
// always-terminating alternative, wired to the same
// analyse_int_dg_eqs_for equation system rather than a separate one, so
// the update rule is a convergence strategy here and not a different
// abstract semantics. Straight-line source keeps the verdict independent
// of that choice: what this pins is that the combination is routed at all
// and returns a real report, on the domain whose join/per-origin support
// was the last to be wired up.
void main() {
  int32 x;
  x := 5;
  __voblint_check(0 < x) // PROVED
}
